# ============================================================================
#  Copy this file to .env  ->  cp .env.example .env  ->  paste your values.
#  The code auto-loads .env (src/_env.py via python-dotenv). You do NOT need
#  to `source .env`. Real environment variables always override these.
#  .env is git-ignored; .env.example (this placeholder) is tracked.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Traccia platform (Phase 2: @govern runtime enforcement + Governance Hub) ----
# Leave BOTH commented to run the three $0 SDK governance beats in LOCAL mode
# (traces write to traces_gov.jsonl; local Tier-A block, PII redaction, and
# EU AI Act / transparency evidence all work with NO key).
#
# Uncomment BOTH to stream to the platform and enable @govern:
#   - key:      app.traccia.ai -> Settings -> API Keys
#   - endpoint: REQUIRED for @govern (without it the SDK logs
#               "Traccia endpoint not found" and SKIPS enforcement -> run returns ALLOWED)
#TRACCIA_API_KEY=your_traccia_api_key_here
#TRACCIA_ENDPOINT=https://api.traccia.ai/v2/traces

# ---- AWS / Bedrock (Amazon Nova Pro) ----
# The crew invokes amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 in us-east-1. Provide AWS creds via your usual
# mechanism (aws configure / SSO / instance role) — do NOT put AWS secrets here.
# Optional overrides:
#AWS_REGION=us-east-1
#LOAN_MODEL_ID=amazon.nova-pro-v1:0

# ---- Optional tuning (safe defaults exist in src/config.py) ----
#LOAN_TEMPERATURE=0.2
#LOAN_MAX_TOKENS=400
#LOAN_MAX_RETRIES=3
#LOAN_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
